{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015oXAoufQL6r2yDh6een8xJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context. Let me proceed with the DREAM review process. I need to:\n\n1. Dispatch R1 (methods + experiments) and R2 (novelty + related work) in parallel\n2. Then conduct a full roundtable: Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-share → Step 3 converge → Step 4 synthesize\n\nLet me first dispatch the two reviewers with their focused tasks.\n\nLet me compose the review tasks for R1 and R2. I need to give them clear, focused assignments.\n\nThe paper is about \"Solver Trace Ablation (STA)\" which introduces a leave-one-out diagnostic (ISR score) for detecting structural degeneration in GRPO-trained formal reasoners. Key claims:\n\n\n- ISR serves as a diagnostic that catches degeneration patterns invisible to prove rate metrics\n- Goodhart's law applies here: using ISR as a reward signal has scale-dependent effects, helping at 4B parameters but hurting at 8B\n- The diagnostic boundaries are mode-dependent, working effectively for chain-of-thought but not for tree search\n\nNow I'll dispatch R1 and R2 with their focused assignments.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25680,"cache_read_input_tokens":24827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25680},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92bb1cac-3ac5-45b9-9e5e-2dcf334b6346","uuid":"c59ab514-1044-415d-b26f-5c58a0c9aa5b"}
